  "worked_solution": "Since $∠SOT$ is straight, $m∠SOT={180}^{∘}.$ So by the angle addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nm∠SOU+m∠UOT={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given expressions into the above, we can solve for $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2z+{60}^{∘})+(3z+{10}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5z+{70}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5z & ={110}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={22}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know $z={22}^{∘},$ we can calculate $m∠SOU$ as follows:\n\n$$\nm∠SOU=2({22}^{∘})+{60}^{∘}={104}^{∘}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the angles $∠SOU$ and $∠TOV$ are vertical angles, they have the same measure:\n\n$$\nm∠TOV=m∠SOU={104}^{∘}\n$$",
